## 🚀 Performance Considerations

### Event Listener Optimization

```tsx
// ✅ Use useCallback for stable handler references
const handleItemSelect = useCallback(
  (event: CustomEvent) => {
    const selectedValue = event.detail?.value;
    // Handle selection
  },
  [theme, setTheme]
); // Dependencies

useEffect(() => {
  const dropdown = dropdownRef.current;
  if (dropdown) {
    dropdown.addEventListener("itemSelect", handleItemSelect);
    return () => {
      dropdown.removeEventListener("itemSelect", handleItemSelect);
    };
  }
}, [handleItemSelect]); // Include callback in dependencies
```

### Conditional Event Attachment

```tsx
useEffect(() => {
  const dropdown = dropdownRef.current;
  if (dropdown && isInteractive) {
    // Only attach when needed
    const handler = (event) => {
      /* handle event */
    };
    dropdown.addEventListener("itemSelect", handler);
    return () => {
      dropdown.removeEventListener("itemSelect", handler);
    };
  }
}, [isInteractive]);
```

## 🔧 Troubleshooting Checklist

When dropdown events aren't working:

- [ ] ✅ **Ref is properly attached**: `ref={dropdownRef}`
- [ ] ✅ **Event listener is attached**: `addEventListener("itemSelect", handler)`
- [ ] ✅ **Cleanup function exists**: `removeEventListener` in return
- [ ] ✅ **Dependencies are correct**: Include all used variables in useEffect deps
- [ ] ✅ **Component is client-side**: `"use client"` directive present
- [ ] ✅ **Hydration is handled**: Mounted state prevents SSR mismatches
- [ ] ✅ **Event name is correct**: Check Modus docs for exact event names
- [ ] ✅ **Debug logs are added**: Console.log to verify event firing
- [ ] ✅ **TypeScript types are correct**: Proper event and ref typing

